# Inert803 metadata operation budget: first stage only

No reader adoption, routes, adapters, SQL, loaders, authorization booleans, payloads, callbacks, providers or DB execution. Existing policy and Finance budgets remain independent and UNCOMPOSED. This central primitive alone does not bound actual reader behavior.

Global engineering limits:1MiB canonical DB JSONB UTF8 bytes,100 distinct cells,1000 total begin attempts per entry. Begin MUST precede every consumer metadata query, including reuse and failed attempts. Existing context entry binds fresh principal object+PK, exact domain set, default connection object and raw connection. New wrappers share state; a new entry starts empty; old tickets cannot cross it. Closed immutable specs contain fixed table/column/identity types/per-cell limits; no arbitrary SQL accepted. Closed selected template-owner domains each maintain independent byte/cell charges, even when another domain already charged a global duplicate. Fingerprint/size/type/identity must match for reuse. Same hash on a different cell charges again.

Metadata and cells are frozen records; no decoded mutable data cache. Tickets transition begun→reserved→validated; downstream errors must call failed (or escape the whole entry). Re-reserving a pending/failed cell cannot count as success. Limit/conflict failures poison the entry and retain charges, with no refunds. Reserved metadata alone is not validated content or authority; consumers still owe native gates and conditional payload transfer. Caller-owned arbitrary Python is not sandboxed; private state/closed registry are trusted internal implementation, not tamper-proof security.

Policy integration pending: add canonical DB fingerprints and remove unsafe reliance on mutable decoded cache. Finance integration pending: use shared ledger before classification, retain local caps and exact gates. Both must condition payload SQL on admitted identity/type/size/fingerprint (or prove no-own-write invariance), because checking after an unconstrained transfer is not prehydration admission. RR alone does not prevent own-transaction writes. Scalar closure and binding/run cardinalities remain separate counters and need explicit attempt composition, not fictitious byte charges. No totalDBwork/RSS or full privacy guarantee.

13 pure tests normal/-O cover cross-domain exact aggregate boundary,100cells, domain/global dedup and lower-cap contrast, identity/fingerprint conflict, conservative failure and unvalidated reservations,1000 shared attempts, context/actor/raw connection rollover, closed specs/PK types, per-cell bounds and immutable metadata. Tests stub only context binding and use fixed metadata; no domain helper or SQL execution. Real fingerprint SQL, canonical byte semantics, permission-before-payload, own-write/concurrency behavior and native fixture integration remain UNRUN. No held code inspected.
